---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/default-no-header.astro";
const title = "Optimizely Design System - Portfolio of Manaj Chakrobarti";
const bodyClass = "works";
import "../../styles/workspages.scss";
---

<PageLayout title={title} bodyClass={bodyClass}>
	<main class="box workspage">
		<header class="inner section-header">
			<h1>
				Redesigning self-service widgets for product recommendations
			</h1>
			<article class="project-information">
				<div class="contributions">
					<h2>My Contributions</h2>
					<ul class="no-list">
						<li>UX/UI Design</li>
						<li>Design System</li>
						<li>Research & Testing</li>
						<li>Heuristic Evaluation</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<section class="details">
					<div class="challange">
						<h2>Challenge</h2>
						<p>
							As our products evolved, maintaining consistency
							across different interfaces became increasingly
							challenging. We needed a shared design system that
							could serve as a reliable reference for designers
							and provide reusable components across products.
						</p>
						<p>
							Over time, we had developed multiple design systems,
							and following the merger with Optimizely, the goal
							was to bring them together into a unified, updated
							system.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="team">
						<h2>Team</h2>
						<p>
							During the NewsCred and Welcome era, three designers
							collectively maintained the design system without a
							dedicated owner. Anyone could propose new components
							or suggest improvements.
						</p>
						<p>
							Following the merger with Optimizely, we began
							integrating our existing system with the Optimizely
							Design System.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="discover">
						<h2>Approch</h2>
						<p>
							We maintained the design system collaboratively,
							reviewing existing components, identifying
							inconsistencies, and exploring opportunities to
							standardize them.
						</p>
						<p>The process involved:</p>
						<ul class="no-list">
							<li>
								<b>Audit:</b> Reviewed existing components across
								products to identify inconsistencies and duplication.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Research:</b> Explored established design systems
								to understand common patterns and best practices.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Design exploration:</b> Developed and refined component
								variations while considering usability and accessibility.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Validation:</b> Involved designers and used preference
								testing to help evaluate design decisions.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Documentation:</b> Updated component guidelines
								to provide a shared reference for designers.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>

					<div class="solution">
						<h2>Solution</h2>
						<p>
							As part of this effort, I worked on standardizing
							badges, which varied across products. I explored
							multiple designs using accessible colors (WCAG AA),
							gathered designers' votes, and selected three
							finalists for user preference testing.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="outcome">
						<h2>Outcome</h2>
						<p>
							The work contributed to a more consistent approach
							to component design and helped move our existing
							design systems towards a unified Optimizely design
							system.
						</p>

						<h2>Learning</h2>
						<p>
							I learned that a design system is not just a
							collection of reusable components. It requires
							collaboration, clear documentation, and continuous
							maintenance to remain useful as products evolve.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</article>
		</header>

		

		<section class="inner">
			<article class="article">
				
				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-design-systems/design_system_screenshot.png"
						alt="Design System"
					/>
					<figcaption>Design System</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>
		</section>
	</main>
</PageLayout>" >
